1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,461
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,545 --> 00:00:07,549
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,591 --> 00:00:10,677
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,762
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:20,228
[Janine] Mommy, I called Daddy,

7
00:00:20,311 --> 00:00:23,189
so my birthday will be our family bonding.

8
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:25,150
[Janine] <i>Why is she here?</i>

9
00:00:25,233 --> 00:00:27,527
Janine, you'll be siblings.
I will adopt her.

10
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:29,320
She needs a mother figure.

11
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:32,073
[in English] You know, someone
who will be… a good role model for her.

12
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:33,324
[Audrey] <i>You should get married.</i>

13
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:34,701
[Leon] If your child is unruly,

14
00:00:34,784 --> 00:00:36,536
don't bring her here just to lose her.

15
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:37,620
Who was that?

16
00:00:37,704 --> 00:00:39,873
- [Gemma] <i>Oh, that was Sir Leon.</i>
- Ouch.

17
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:41,374
- Son of a… So stupid.
- [indistinct]

18
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:43,334
I apologize on her behalf.

19
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:47,630
If you and Sir Delfin
were single back then,

20
00:00:47,714 --> 00:00:49,674
do you think you could've been together?

21
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:51,342
[Karla] I wish that were the case, right?

22
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:53,636
Then Brother Atoy
and I would be your children.

23
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:56,681
- [Ame] Mm-hmm.
- There's a horseback riding activity here.

24
00:00:57,223 --> 00:00:58,975
I want to ride a horse.

25
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:01,644
You go ahead. I'll just change. Okay?

26
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:03,063
[in English] Yes!

27
00:01:03,772 --> 00:01:05,356
[Audrey] <i>Atoy! Atoy!</i>

28
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,317
Don't leave yet. Stay here first.

29
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:11,237
Um, Janine requested that
we surprise her with a birthday cake.

30
00:01:11,321 --> 00:01:13,865
[in English] <i>Don't forget to make a wish</i>
<i>before you blow your candle, my child.</i>

31
00:01:13,948 --> 00:01:16,868
[Janine] <i>I wish my parents</i>
<i>would get back together,</i>

32
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:18,995
<i>so our family of three will be complete!</i>

33
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:20,205
Audrey?

34
00:01:20,288 --> 00:01:22,207
I know how to swim.

35
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:24,042
I lived on the island for a long time.

36
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:25,126
Are you alone?

37
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:27,170
I'm waiting for my father.

38
00:01:27,253 --> 00:01:28,296
He's taking so long.

39
00:01:28,379 --> 00:01:29,464
Kiss each other, please.

40
00:01:29,547 --> 00:01:30,423
- Kiss.
- Hey, she's asking for a kiss.

41
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:31,841
[staff, in English] One, two, three!

42
00:01:31,925 --> 00:01:33,635
Oh, one more. One more.

43
00:01:33,718 --> 00:01:34,928
[Atoy] <i>One, two. Mmm, mmm, mmm.</i>

44
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:36,387
PREVIOUSLY

45
00:01:36,471 --> 00:01:37,347
Okay.

46
00:01:37,430 --> 00:01:40,725
[music fades]

47
00:01:40,809 --> 00:01:42,852
- [Janine] Mommy.
- Hmm?

48
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:46,189
Do you still have feelings for Daddy?

49
00:01:46,272 --> 00:01:49,734
- [light music playing]
- [chuckles]

50
00:01:49,818 --> 00:01:51,611
What are you saying, Ibyang?

51
00:01:52,737 --> 00:01:56,825
Because you and Aunt Audrey
look good together!

52
00:01:57,408 --> 00:01:59,160
When you adopt me,

53
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:01,955
and you're looking for a mother for me,

54
00:02:02,038 --> 00:02:05,542
Aunt Audrey is a big check for me!

55
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:08,711
Can't you get back together?

56
00:02:08,795 --> 00:02:12,257
Maybe you still love each other.

57
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:14,217
That was before, child.

58
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:16,886
But I think…

59
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:19,973
Daddy still has a crush on you.

60
00:02:20,056 --> 00:02:22,392
- Oh, Janine!
- [giggles]

61
00:02:22,475 --> 00:02:23,560
[Audrey sighs]

62
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:24,561
Oh.

63
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:28,398
- Tatoy is blushing!
- [quirky flourish]

64
00:02:28,481 --> 00:02:30,191
- [Ibyang] Hmm, hmm.
- What blush? That's sunburn!

65
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:31,234
See, it's so hot.

66
00:02:31,317 --> 00:02:33,736
Oh, you! Hmm, hmm!

67
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:39,033
It's obvious you still have feelings
for Aunt Audrey!

68
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:41,619
Just court her.

69
00:02:42,162 --> 00:02:44,497
You're both single anyway.

70
00:02:46,749 --> 00:02:48,001
No.

71
00:02:48,084 --> 00:02:49,544
We're fine like this.

72
00:02:49,627 --> 00:02:51,754
We're friends for Janine's sake.

73
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:56,217
Mommy, I know you love me so much, but…

74
00:02:56,301 --> 00:03:00,263
I still want a happy family,
with all three of us complete.

75
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:03,766
Because until now,
I haven't really experienced that.

76
00:03:05,894 --> 00:03:07,729
[in English] I want that
for you too, child.

77
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:10,690
[in English] But it's not that simple.

78
00:03:10,773 --> 00:03:13,902
[suave theme music playing]

79
00:03:16,237 --> 00:03:18,072
[motorcycle revving]

80
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:19,490
[sewing machine whirring]

81
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:21,993
[snipping]

82
00:03:24,537 --> 00:03:25,872
[sewing machine clacking]

83
00:03:25,955 --> 00:03:27,790
- [gun cocks]
- [gunfire]

84
00:03:27,874 --> 00:03:29,250
[gunfire blasting]

85
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:31,544
[clicking]

86
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:33,630
[snipping]

87
00:03:36,674 --> 00:03:39,260
[electronic blipping]

88
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:44,933
[crickets chirping]

89
00:03:46,142 --> 00:03:47,352
[Ibyang] Ouch!

90
00:03:47,435 --> 00:03:49,187
[soft moan]

91
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:51,314
- [Ibyang] It hurts.
- You're overreacting.

92
00:03:51,397 --> 00:03:53,524
It doesn't hurt that much.

93
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:55,443
[Ibyang] Why are you bothering me?

94
00:03:56,069 --> 00:03:58,488
I kept my promise.

95
00:03:59,197 --> 00:04:02,575
I'm letting you bond
with your mommy and daddy.

96
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:07,288
Here, throw this.

97
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:09,290
Let's play. Come on.

98
00:04:09,374 --> 00:04:10,541
‪[gentle music playing]

99
00:04:11,209 --> 00:04:12,460
Come on.

100
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:13,962
[swooshes]

101
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,882
- [chuckles]
- [Janine] You're laughing, huh.

102
00:04:20,426 --> 00:04:22,553
Me too. Catch this.

103
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:28,518
[swooshes]

104
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:29,852
[clatters]

105
00:04:30,436 --> 00:04:32,021
- That's the grumpy man.
- [Leon] Hey!

106
00:04:32,897 --> 00:04:34,732
Let's go.

107
00:04:35,608 --> 00:04:37,819
[tense music playing]

108
00:04:37,902 --> 00:04:38,903
You two!

109
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:41,197
Where are you going?!

110
00:04:41,864 --> 00:04:43,908
She's the one She's the one
who threw it, not me!

111
00:04:43,992 --> 00:04:44,867
Me?

112
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:45,743
- [Leon] You--
- [Janine] Yes, you!

113
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:47,453
You lying child!

114
00:04:47,537 --> 00:04:48,538
- Come here!
- Ouch!

115
00:04:49,122 --> 00:04:51,249
I saw you. You threw it!

116
00:04:51,332 --> 00:04:52,917
And now you're blaming your playmate?!

117
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:55,003
You're a lying child, huh!

118
00:04:55,086 --> 00:04:56,087
[cracks]

119
00:04:56,170 --> 00:05:00,341
[music intensifies]

120
00:05:00,425 --> 00:05:01,718
She didn't mean it.

121
00:05:03,636 --> 00:05:06,848
You! I'm just scaring you!

122
00:05:06,931 --> 00:05:08,308
So you'll learn your lesson.

123
00:05:08,391 --> 00:05:09,559
And stay away from my cabin!

124
00:05:10,184 --> 00:05:11,602
I'll tell my mommy and daddy.

125
00:05:11,686 --> 00:05:13,271
You're a bad person!

126
00:05:13,354 --> 00:05:14,689
[in English] Good!

127
00:05:14,772 --> 00:05:16,316
Bring them here,

128
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:18,735
so I can smack them with your frisbee!

129
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:20,570
Go on!

130
00:05:20,653 --> 00:05:25,199
[music fades]

131
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:29,203
[Audrey, in English] Girls! Uh,
dinner is ready at the dining hall.

132
00:05:29,287 --> 00:05:30,246
Oh, what happened to you, my dear?

133
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,498
Mommy, there was a man there.

134
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:35,001
He broke our frisbee, then pinched me.

135
00:05:35,084 --> 00:05:36,669
And who was that man?

136
00:05:36,753 --> 00:05:38,129
Janine, you were not--

137
00:05:38,212 --> 00:05:40,089
That-- That mean man.

138
00:05:40,173 --> 00:05:41,591
He said

139
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:43,885
I should bring you and Daddy to his cabin,

140
00:05:43,968 --> 00:05:46,012
so he could smack you with the frisbee.

141
00:05:46,095 --> 00:05:47,638
Wait, I'll talk to him.

142
00:05:47,722 --> 00:05:50,349
Go to the dining hall, okay.
Atoy is there.

143
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:52,894
Aunt Audrey, don't go to him!

144
00:05:52,977 --> 00:05:54,562
[tense music playing]

145
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:57,440
Tatoy needs to know.

146
00:05:57,523 --> 00:05:58,357
Huh?

147
00:05:59,358 --> 00:06:00,651
Ibyang!

148
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:04,113
[tense music playing]

149
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:17,919
- Anybody home?
- [knock on door]

150
00:06:18,002 --> 00:06:18,878
[Audrey] Hello?

151
00:06:18,961 --> 00:06:21,339
- [knock on door]
- [Audrey] Hello!

152
00:06:21,422 --> 00:06:22,799
It's open. Come in!

153
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:24,467
[music fades]

154
00:06:27,595 --> 00:06:29,722
[mysterious music playing]

155
00:06:33,392 --> 00:06:35,019
So, it's you.

156
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:38,272
I was the one who asked you earlier.

157
00:06:38,356 --> 00:06:39,607
What do you want?

158
00:06:42,777 --> 00:06:44,362
[Audrey] I'll be direct with you.

159
00:06:45,321 --> 00:06:47,615
I didn't like what you did to my child.

160
00:06:48,991 --> 00:06:50,326
What's your problem?

161
00:06:50,409 --> 00:06:53,412
Ah. You're the mother of that child.

162
00:06:54,997 --> 00:06:58,751
No wonder she's unruly,
because you neglected her!

163
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:00,586
[in English] Excuse me?

164
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:02,505
You're the one at fault.

165
00:07:02,588 --> 00:07:05,716
You broke their toy,
and you hurt my child!

166
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,969
[in English] You know,
I could sue you for child abuse!

167
00:07:08,052 --> 00:07:09,428
You're arrogant.

168
00:07:09,512 --> 00:07:11,222
You think you're somebody.

169
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:15,059
[rousing music playing]

170
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:16,561
Do you want to know me?

171
00:07:18,354 --> 00:07:20,648
Do you think I'm afraid of you?

172
00:07:21,232 --> 00:07:22,233
You should be.

173
00:07:23,401 --> 00:07:26,112
Because I'll be the last person
you'll ever see in your life.

174
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:27,780
[gun cocks]

175
00:07:27,864 --> 00:07:30,199
[foreboding music playing]

176
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:43,421
I'm sorry for the things I said.

177
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:49,427
Um, this doesn't need to go this far.

178
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:51,304
Why did mommy suddenly act nice?

179
00:07:54,056 --> 00:07:56,100
That's why there are unruly children,

180
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:58,019
- because of people like you!
- [Audrey, in English] I'm sorry.

181
00:07:58,102 --> 00:08:00,354
Uh-uh, c-can we just…

182
00:08:00,438 --> 00:08:02,106
forget about it?

183
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:03,357
Come here.

184
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:06,611
Come closer. Closer.

185
00:08:07,778 --> 00:08:09,530
- Come closer!
- Ouch [groans]

186
00:08:09,614 --> 00:08:10,490
[gasps]

187
00:08:10,573 --> 00:08:12,241
[Audrey] Please, please.

188
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:13,743
[music swells]

189
00:08:13,826 --> 00:08:15,411
- Come here!
- [groans]

190
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:23,961
[dramatic sting]

191
00:08:24,045 --> 00:08:27,298
- [tense music playing]
- [gasping]

192
00:08:27,381 --> 00:08:29,008
Is that daddy?

193
00:08:29,091 --> 00:08:30,760
- What? Did you send for him?
- [sharp inhale]

194
00:08:30,843 --> 00:08:31,719
Hmm?!

195
00:08:33,054 --> 00:08:33,888
‪No.

196
00:08:34,889 --> 00:08:37,183
- Sit, sit!
- [gasping]

197
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:47,360
‪[dramatic sting]

198
00:08:54,492 --> 00:08:55,326
‪[dramatic sting]

199
00:08:56,827 --> 00:09:00,331
Let's go to that mean man.
Daddy will deal with him.

200
00:09:01,082 --> 00:09:03,584
Janine, let's not go there.

201
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:06,045
That man is dangerous.

202
00:09:06,128 --> 00:09:07,421
He has a gun!

203
00:09:07,505 --> 00:09:10,675
A gun? You're exaggerating. He doesn't.
You're making it up.

204
00:09:11,342 --> 00:09:12,218
Hmm?

205
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:14,720
I saw it earlier.

206
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:19,350
You even said he pinched you,
but he didn't.

207
00:09:19,433 --> 00:09:22,520
Yes, but he almost hit me.

208
00:09:22,603 --> 00:09:24,063
That's the same thing.

209
00:09:24,146 --> 00:09:25,439
[dramatic sting]

210
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:26,357
[Atoy] Audrey?

211
00:09:27,483 --> 00:09:28,442
Audrey!

212
00:09:29,068 --> 00:09:30,236
Come in!

213
00:09:30,319 --> 00:09:32,822
[door clicks open]

214
00:09:32,905 --> 00:09:35,783
[ominous music playing]

215
00:09:35,866 --> 00:09:36,867
Audrey?

216
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:41,080
Are you her husband?

217
00:09:41,789 --> 00:09:42,623
‪[dramatic sting]

218
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:48,588
We were just talking
about what your child did earlier.

219
00:09:48,671 --> 00:09:50,464
Oh, well, I'll stay with her.

220
00:09:50,548 --> 00:09:52,508
Ah-- [in English] No, Atoy. I'm good.

221
00:09:54,176 --> 00:09:58,973
[ominous music playing]

222
00:10:05,563 --> 00:10:07,356
I'm the father of the child.

223
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:09,900
Maybe the two of us should talk instead.

224
00:10:11,402 --> 00:10:13,195
We've been talking for a while.

225
00:10:14,530 --> 00:10:17,241
I don't want to repeat what I said,

226
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:19,201
so you can leave now.

227
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:21,746
[dramatic sting]

228
00:10:21,829 --> 00:10:24,123
Ah, okay.

229
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:29,503
[tense sting]

230
00:10:30,087 --> 00:10:31,797
[Atoy] This cabin is beautiful.

231
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:34,008
So fancy.

232
00:10:34,508 --> 00:10:35,968
So spacious, right?

233
00:10:36,802 --> 00:10:37,678
[in English] Wow.

234
00:10:38,304 --> 00:10:40,473
[tense sting]

235
00:10:45,645 --> 00:10:47,813
- [Audrey screams] Atoy!
- [gunfire]

236
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:49,106
[gunfire in distance]

237
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:50,191
What's that?

238
00:10:51,567 --> 00:10:54,820
That's gunfire. Let's get help.

239
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:55,946
Okay, okay.

240
00:10:57,406 --> 00:10:58,407
[gunfire]

241
00:10:59,408 --> 00:11:01,118
- [Audrey squeals] Atoy!
- Quick! Come with me!

242
00:11:01,202 --> 00:11:02,453
[groans]

243
00:11:02,536 --> 00:11:03,537
Don't follow!

244
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:05,247
- I'll kill her!
- [shrieks]

245
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:08,209
[Audrey gasping]

246
00:11:10,461 --> 00:11:13,005
- Atoy!
- [gunfire]

247
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:16,217
- [gunfire]
- [squeals]

248
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:17,134
‪[Audrey gasping]

249
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:19,678
[foreboding music playing]

250
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:21,555
- [Audrey shrieks, gasping]
- Hurry up!

251
00:11:21,639 --> 00:11:23,557
Let me go. If you're escaping, uh, you--

252
00:11:23,641 --> 00:11:25,434
You don't need to take me.

253
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:26,644
Please, don't take me.

254
00:11:27,895 --> 00:11:29,313
Looks like you have a car.

255
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:34,193
- Come on, drive for me!
- S-Sorry. I didn't bring my car keys.

256
00:11:34,276 --> 00:11:35,111
You're useless!

257
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:37,696
[shrieks, gasping]

258
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:38,823
[Atoy] Sir!

259
00:11:40,282 --> 00:11:41,158
Sir…

260
00:11:42,451 --> 00:11:44,703
Sir, I'll go with you.

261
00:11:45,204 --> 00:11:46,997
I don't trust you!

262
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:51,127
I'll help you. Sir, please.

263
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:53,295
Sir, I don't want my child
to lose her mother.

264
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:55,339
Do you have a car?

265
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:57,383
- Yes.
- Where's the key?

266
00:11:57,466 --> 00:12:00,469
[ominous music playing]

267
00:12:00,553 --> 00:12:02,763
Let's go. Drive for me!

268
00:12:06,267 --> 00:12:07,560
- [groans]
- [squeals]

269
00:12:08,561 --> 00:12:10,062
[grunting and groaning]

270
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,523
[groans]

271
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:20,865
[security guard] Stop!

272
00:12:20,948 --> 00:12:23,033
[groaning]

273
00:12:23,742 --> 00:12:25,786
[grunts]

274
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:26,996
[grunts]

275
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:28,706
[gasps]

276
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:30,541
Thank you, Atoy.

277
00:12:30,624 --> 00:12:32,376
[sharp exhale]

278
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:36,797
[melancholic music playing]

279
00:12:46,515 --> 00:12:49,602
Sir, the suspect Leon Torres
has long had an arrest warrant

280
00:12:49,685 --> 00:12:50,978
for homicide in Cavite.

281
00:12:51,061 --> 00:12:53,564
He went into hiding
and was only arrested now.

282
00:12:54,648 --> 00:12:56,525
- Thank you.
- Thank you as well.

283
00:12:57,109 --> 00:12:58,486
- We'll go ahead.
- All right.

284
00:12:58,569 --> 00:13:01,655
[crickets chirping]

285
00:13:01,739 --> 00:13:02,865
[Janine] Mommy!

286
00:13:02,948 --> 00:13:04,742
Are you okay?

287
00:13:04,825 --> 00:13:06,410
I'm-- I'm-- I'm safe, dear.

288
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:09,038
Your daddy saved me.

289
00:13:10,122 --> 00:13:12,082
[Ibyang] My Tatoy is amazing.

290
00:13:12,166 --> 00:13:14,084
So cool!

291
00:13:14,168 --> 00:13:15,503
[pensive music playing]

292
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:16,795
Are you okay?

293
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:17,796
I know he hurt you.

294
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:19,423
[in English] I-I'm fine. I'm fine.

295
00:13:20,174 --> 00:13:22,259
Do you want to go
to the hospital, see a doctor?

296
00:13:22,343 --> 00:13:25,054
[in English] It's--
It's been a long day, Atoy.

297
00:13:26,138 --> 00:13:27,932
Let's all rest.

298
00:13:28,641 --> 00:13:29,767
Come on, dear.

299
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:52,915
[Karla] Mom, you've been quiet.

300
00:13:53,457 --> 00:13:55,209
Are you upset with Sister Ame?

301
00:13:55,292 --> 00:13:56,335
Not really.

302
00:13:57,378 --> 00:14:00,673
Karla, maybe don't mention Delfin's name,

303
00:14:00,756 --> 00:14:02,925
especially in front of your father.

304
00:14:03,842 --> 00:14:06,554
Why? Is he insecure about my godfather?

305
00:14:08,305 --> 00:14:10,057
- [sighs]
- [Nestor] Karla.

306
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:14,895
I saw your father drinking at the corner
with Willie, carrying liquor.

307
00:14:14,979 --> 00:14:16,814
His buddy from Saudi.

308
00:14:16,897 --> 00:14:18,232
I'm just telling you, okay.

309
00:14:18,315 --> 00:14:21,485
Don't say I didn't try to stop him
from buying alcohol.

310
00:14:21,569 --> 00:14:22,903
What time was he there?

311
00:14:22,987 --> 00:14:25,322
Around two in the afternoon.

312
00:14:25,406 --> 00:14:27,825
Mom, I thought he was looking for work?

313
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:29,535
Turns out he was just
drinking at the corner.

314
00:14:29,618 --> 00:14:30,953
Come with me to see your father.

315
00:14:31,036 --> 00:14:33,998
Leave him there. Let him sleep there.

316
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:35,165
[sighs]

317
00:14:35,249 --> 00:14:36,417
Come with me.

318
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:38,502
I'll really hit Noel this time.

319
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:39,503
Let's go.

320
00:14:40,296 --> 00:14:42,965
[rousing music playing]

321
00:14:44,008 --> 00:14:48,429
[crickets chirping]

322
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:02,610
Here.

323
00:15:03,986 --> 00:15:06,780
Put this on. It will swell.

324
00:15:08,782 --> 00:15:09,992
Thank you.

325
00:15:17,207 --> 00:15:18,375
So…

326
00:15:18,459 --> 00:15:20,085
[crickets chirping]

327
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:22,796
What are you still doing here?

328
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:24,673
I thought you wanted to rest?

329
00:15:27,718 --> 00:15:29,261
I can't sleep.

330
00:15:32,014 --> 00:15:33,182
I keep thinking…

331
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:36,644
What if…

332
00:15:37,603 --> 00:15:39,855
something worse happened?

333
00:15:41,732 --> 00:15:42,983
Then I'd be dead.

334
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:46,362
You'd be alive. [inhales]

335
00:15:46,445 --> 00:15:47,696
That's better.

336
00:15:48,489 --> 00:15:52,660
At least Janine would still have
a mother. Right?

337
00:15:55,287 --> 00:15:57,373
That's kind of how we are anyway.

338
00:15:57,456 --> 00:16:01,043
[inhales] Think about it,
after all those years apart.

339
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:03,837
[smirks] Eight years, right?

340
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:07,132
It's like we were dead to each other.

341
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:12,805
It's different now.

342
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:17,893
What do you mean?

343
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:21,605
Nothing. Um…

344
00:16:23,691 --> 00:16:24,984
I-I'll just go inside--

345
00:16:25,067 --> 00:16:28,737
[gentle music playing]

346
00:16:29,446 --> 00:16:30,572
What do you mean?

347
00:16:35,869 --> 00:16:36,912
You don't want to lose me again?

348
00:16:38,747 --> 00:16:40,040
Why can't you say it?

349
00:16:42,501 --> 00:16:46,547
I don't want our child to lose her father.

350
00:16:50,342 --> 00:16:51,552
[Audrey clears throat]

351
00:16:56,098 --> 00:16:57,599
Is that really the only reason?

352
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:02,604
Or do you still want me?

353
00:17:04,023 --> 00:17:08,235
[sentimental music playing]

354
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:12,156
[scoffs, in English] Of course not!

355
00:17:14,074 --> 00:17:15,784
[sighs, then titters]

356
00:17:16,785 --> 00:17:18,120
Then why did you have me tracked?

357
00:17:19,246 --> 00:17:21,623
[inhales] Why did you want
the tracker to look for me,

358
00:17:22,541 --> 00:17:24,209
even though your father
didn't want you to?

359
00:17:25,502 --> 00:17:27,379
I know you were looking for me.

360
00:17:27,463 --> 00:17:29,256
It's none of your business.

361
00:17:30,549 --> 00:17:32,009
[gentle music playing]

362
00:17:32,092 --> 00:17:35,179
Audrey, we're not on the island anymore.

363
00:17:35,262 --> 00:17:37,806
We're not on the island to fool around.

364
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:39,308
[chuckles softly]

365
00:17:39,391 --> 00:17:40,392
So, why?

366
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:42,352
Why were you searching for me?

367
00:17:44,646 --> 00:17:45,689
[in English] Closure?

368
00:17:47,024 --> 00:17:48,400
[in English] Second chance?

369
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:55,741
[Willie] Drink up.

370
00:17:57,034 --> 00:17:58,285
Oh, ice, more ice!

371
00:18:00,704 --> 00:18:02,456
- Mmm.
- Ice, ice!

372
00:18:02,539 --> 00:18:04,708
- Oh.
- It makes drinking better.

373
00:18:04,792 --> 00:18:07,503
- Hey, the ice!
- That's too big!

374
00:18:07,586 --> 00:18:09,088
- Break it.
- Break it down.

375
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:10,380
[Cita] Noel!

376
00:18:10,464 --> 00:18:13,258
- Here.
- What's this?!

377
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:16,303
I gave you money because
you said you'd look for a job.

378
00:18:16,386 --> 00:18:18,430
Turns out you're just drinking!

379
00:18:19,014 --> 00:18:21,141
This is called networking!

380
00:18:21,725 --> 00:18:25,104
Willie will find me a job in Riyadh!

381
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:30,067
Noel, it's better if you start
a business here.

382
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:35,239
Don't take a job that will keep you
away for so long.

383
00:18:35,322 --> 00:18:37,199
You don't know. Maybe…

384
00:18:37,282 --> 00:18:40,828
someone's hovering around Cita. [laughs]

385
00:18:40,911 --> 00:18:42,287
Cita?!

386
00:18:42,371 --> 00:18:44,790
Eh-- She's old already! No one would--

387
00:18:44,873 --> 00:18:46,750
You even insulted me! Go home!

388
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:48,377
[Willie] Back then,

389
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:51,421
you don't even know.
Maybe Delfin stole her away.

390
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:55,008
You know, tailors are sharp, like needles.

391
00:18:55,092 --> 00:18:56,635
Sharp! [laughs]

392
00:18:56,718 --> 00:18:57,553
You bastard!

393
00:18:57,636 --> 00:18:59,346
- [bottle shatters]
- [groans]

394
00:18:59,429 --> 00:19:02,182
That's a bad joke! That's a bad joke!

395
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:04,268
Run, you animal!

396
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:06,645
You'll be picking your guts off
the street!

397
00:19:06,728 --> 00:19:08,647
- [indistinct]
- [shouts]

398
00:19:08,730 --> 00:19:10,107
[Nestor] Stop it!

399
00:19:10,899 --> 00:19:13,026
- Step aside, Nestor!
- No! Stop it!

400
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:14,194
Step aside!

401
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:16,071
[growls]

402
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:17,990
[tense music playing]

403
00:19:18,073 --> 00:19:21,076
[gasping]

404
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:26,373
When we were on the island…

405
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:29,626
[sighs]

406
00:19:30,502 --> 00:19:31,503
I came back for you.

407
00:19:33,881 --> 00:19:34,798
[Atoy] <i>You were gone.</i>

408
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:38,093
<i>Then I saw the necklace I gave you,</i>

409
00:19:38,177 --> 00:19:40,429
<i>you just threw it in the trash.</i>

410
00:19:41,722 --> 00:19:42,890
[sighs]

411
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:45,642
I'll admit, I got hurt.

412
00:19:45,726 --> 00:19:49,104
[gentle music playing]

413
00:19:50,397 --> 00:19:52,107
Because maybe I did love you.

414
00:19:53,483 --> 00:19:55,944
I didn't throw away your necklace.

415
00:19:57,321 --> 00:19:58,822
I was holding it.

416
00:20:00,199 --> 00:20:02,826
I waited for you because I wanted you.

417
00:20:05,495 --> 00:20:07,623
[Audrey] <i>But my father's men took me.</i>

418
00:20:12,419 --> 00:20:14,546
Then I was in a coma.

419
00:20:15,047 --> 00:20:17,257
They brought me to the States and--

420
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:20,052
[sobbing]

421
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:24,723
That's why I was gone for so long.

422
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:29,144
[sobs]

423
00:20:29,645 --> 00:20:31,772
Why are you only telling me this now?

424
00:20:31,855 --> 00:20:33,232
[Audrey] I don't know!

425
00:20:33,732 --> 00:20:36,235
And yes, that's why I had you tracked.

426
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:38,820
Because I wanted to know
if you were still alive.

427
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:43,909
If you had another family.
If-- If you still felt something for me.

428
00:20:43,992 --> 00:20:46,370
[gentle music playing]

429
00:20:46,453 --> 00:20:48,163
I even had a necklace made

430
00:20:48,247 --> 00:20:50,624
so I wouldn't forget you!

431
00:20:57,172 --> 00:20:58,715
But when I saw you…

432
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:01,093
[sobs]

433
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:02,970
I held back because…

434
00:21:03,637 --> 00:21:06,348
[sniffles] It seemed
like I didn't matter to you.

435
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:11,728
Then I thought you were with Tonet.

436
00:21:11,812 --> 00:21:14,481
[dramatic sting]

437
00:21:17,317 --> 00:21:19,236
[Audrey] <i>I was just holding</i>
<i>myself back, Atoy.</i>

438
00:21:19,319 --> 00:21:21,571
But I was hurting.

439
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:28,453
[sentimental music playing]

440
00:21:30,455 --> 00:21:31,665
Audrey.

441
00:21:38,797 --> 00:21:42,342
You know, even if it felt like…

442
00:21:44,344 --> 00:21:46,805
like just a one-night stand between us…

443
00:21:50,892 --> 00:21:52,477
I never forgot you.

444
00:21:55,188 --> 00:21:56,857
That's why, when we met again,

445
00:21:59,401 --> 00:22:01,153
it felt like I came alive again.

446
00:22:05,282 --> 00:22:07,034
Audrey, I never loved anyone else…

447
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:10,120
since then.

448
00:22:14,041 --> 00:22:15,250
Atoy,

449
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:19,838
I'm not the same Elaine
you met on the island…

450
00:22:21,381 --> 00:22:24,176
to fall foolishly for you again.

451
00:22:27,095 --> 00:22:28,764
Yes, I met people.

452
00:22:30,974 --> 00:22:33,393
But I looked for you in all of them.

453
00:22:36,354 --> 00:22:37,606
That's why none of them lasted.

454
00:23:05,383 --> 00:23:07,844
[sentimental music playing]

455
00:23:07,928 --> 00:23:10,013
- [sighs]
- [in English] I'm sorry.

456
00:23:12,307 --> 00:23:13,225
[clears throat]

457
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:40,377
[keys jingling, then thuds]

458
00:24:01,439 --> 00:24:05,277
[sentimental music playing]

459
00:24:08,989 --> 00:24:15,829
[electronic blipping]

460
00:24:19,708 --> 00:24:21,293
[Noel] Maybe you're forgetting!

461
00:24:21,376 --> 00:24:23,837
I accepted you,
even with all your nonsense!

462
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:27,674
- That's over!
- But the evidence, it's still there!

463
00:24:27,757 --> 00:24:29,676
I see it every day!

464
00:24:29,759 --> 00:24:32,012
Playing basketball all the time!

465
00:24:32,095 --> 00:24:33,388
And gives me a headache!

466
00:24:33,471 --> 00:24:36,224
You can't sit here. Find another table.

467
00:24:36,308 --> 00:24:38,727
But I want to be with Tatoy here.

468
00:24:38,810 --> 00:24:40,979
And I just want to eat.

469
00:24:44,149 --> 00:24:45,525
I'm still not comfortable with that Atoy.

470
00:24:45,609 --> 00:24:47,402
We can't do anything, hon.

471
00:24:47,485 --> 00:24:50,071
[in English] As long as they're only
doing co-parenting, we're…

472
00:24:50,155 --> 00:24:51,281
we're safe for now.

473
00:24:51,364 --> 00:24:52,574
[in English] You're not sure.

474
00:24:52,657 --> 00:24:54,492
[Red] <i>What if they get back together?</i>

475
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:55,827
UP NEXT

476
00:24:55,911 --> 00:25:00,415
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

477
00:25:04,586 --> 00:25:06,713
♪ <i>Oh, mister, oh, mister</i> ♪

478
00:25:06,796 --> 00:25:10,467
♪ <i>Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

479
00:25:10,550 --> 00:25:14,304
- [electronic blipping]
- [music swells]

480
00:25:14,387 --> 00:25:16,473
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
